  "conclusion": "Observed biological change is real, but by itself it does not establish universal common ancestry or show that unguided mechanisms can explain the information, machinery, and origin of life.",
  "thread": "The design lessons raised questions about the origin of life. This bonus study looks at how observed biological changes, claims about common ancestry, and our worldview fit into that discussion.",
  "bigIdea": "Populations change, and natural selection happens. But common ancestry, the limits of natural processes, and the origin of life raise further questions. We should examine each claim on its evidence.",
